  "review_description": "Seventeen final controls pass; native reference/empty/blind-GLM rewards are 1/0/1 without exceptions. One quality revision resolves the public question, then repeats independent computation, controls and final review. GLM removes an unused packaged expected HMM and revalidates the environment. Supplemental inspection of exact installed test sources is bounded, not a proof against all answer exposure. The independent implementation and solver share the PyHMMER/HMMER engine: cross-engine portability, biological validity and broad factory reliability remain unproven. Original MIT, Pfam CC0 and UniProt CC BY 4.0 notices are retained. The upstream advisory label remains unverified because this uses the separate BioTasks scientific acceptance workflow.",
